{"ref":"BDB, יְבֵ֫מֶת","hw":"יְבֵ֫מֶת","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">יְבֵ֫מֶת</span>]</big>  <strong>n.f. sister-in-law (</strong>NH <span dir=\"rtl\">יְבָמָה</span>, 𝔗 <span dir=\"rtl\">יְבַמְתָּא</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">יְבִימְתָּא</span>; Syriac <span dir=\"rtl\">ܝܺܒܰܡܬܳܐ</span> <strong>)</strong>—only sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">יְבִמְתּוֹ</span> <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 25:7\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.25.7\">Dt 25:7</a><sup>(×2)</sup>, <a data-ref=\"Deuteronomy 9\" href=\"/Deuteronomy.9\">9</a> <em>his brother’s wife</em> (<em>widow</em>), (cf. <a data-ref=\"Genesis 38:8\" href=\"/Genesis.38.8\">Gn 38:8</a>) in levirate law; <span dir=\"rtl\">יְבִמְתֵּךְ</span> <a data-ref=\"Ruth 1:15\" href=\"/Ruth.1.15\">Ru 1:15</a><sup>(×2)</sup> <em>thy husband’s brother’s wife</em>.","next":"BDB, יָבַם","prev":"BDB, יָבָם"}